traces.answer:
So I’ve been doing this “SaaStr + AI” series now with some great guests:
Founder & CEO @owner.com
CEO
@Gong_io
Co-Founder &
@SuperhumanHQ
CEO
@Dialpad
CTO
@Box
VPS
@gainsighthq
CMO
@mangomint
COO
@Billcom
VP Product
@Asana
and more! What I’ve learned is the answers vary widely, depending who you talk to. Some see massive disruption. Others see things getting better, just like before. And others see little change overall. Let’s dig in. The best answer came from founder / CEO of Owner.com,
Michael Burry
, which we’ll get to below. But let me summarize what my learnings were. First, many CMOs seem to think they’ll be replaced by AI soon, if they aren’t already. Many told us at SaaStr Annual that their jobs won’t exist much longer. Second, folks working in support tell us they’re overwhelmed today. They don’t really see any help coming anytime soon. Third, founders tell me they don’t want to hire anyone anymore. Not sales reps. Not marketers. Nothing. It seems too expensive, too risky, etc. This might lead one to believe that AI will radically improve how business software works. That everyone will win here. But no. Here’s why. Because AI makes so many jobs harder. We asked the CEOs of Gong, Super Human, Dialpad, Box, Gainsight, MangoMint and Bill (more on them
here
) what parts of B2B would become easier with AI, and the honest truth was none of these leaders thought anything would truly become dramatically easier.

